---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { release, downloadUrl } from '../data/releases';
const chromeUrl = downloadUrl(release.downloads.chrome);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Slate Support | Slate"
  description="Help with Slate for Windows, browser capture, Quick Search, and Merge."
  home={false}
>
  <article class="shell privacy-page support-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">SLATE / SUPPORT</p>
    <h1>Slate Support</h1>
    <p class="privacy-intro">
      Help with installing Slate, saving from Chrome, and finding your clips.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Install <a href="/download/windows/">Slate for Windows</a> for your
          Windows account. Choose x64 for Intel/AMD PCs or ARM64 for
          Windows-on-ARM PCs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Install the{' '}
          {chromeUrl ? (
            <a href={chromeUrl}>Slate Chrome extension</a>
          ) : (
            'Slate Chrome extension'
          )}{' '}
          from the Chrome Web Store.
        </li>
        <li>
          Keep the Slate desktop app installed. Browser capture requires it.
        </li>
        <li>Save from Chrome to your local Slate library.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        The installer supplies the native host that saves browser captures
        locally, without the desktop window relaying each capture. Open Slate to
        view your library. The extension is optional for creating, editing and
        searching clips directly in Slate Desktop.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Verify your installer</h2>
      <p>
        Use only official Slate downloads. Compare the installer's SHA-256 with
        its matching filename in <strong>SHA256SUMS.txt</strong> on the{' '}
        <a
          href={`${site.repositoryUrl}/releases/latest`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          latest official GitHub release
        </a>
        . Current installers are not Authenticode-signed, so Windows may show
        Unknown Publisher. Tauri updater signatures are separate from Windows
        publisher certificates. Proceed past a SmartScreen reputation warning
        only after checking the official source and checksum; do not bypass
        malware detections or organizational restrictions or disable Windows
        protection.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Saving from Chrome</h2>
      <p>
        Select useful text, right-click, and choose{' '}
        <strong>Save selection</strong>. Use <strong>Save this page</strong> to
        keep the page's link and title. On supported ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini
        pages, you can also use the selection's <strong>Save</strong> action.
      </p>
      <p>Source links and page context are retained where available.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Quick Search</h2>
      <p>
        Press{' '}
        <span class="support-shortcut">
          <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd>
        </span>{' '}
        while Slate is running to find saved clips without navigating the full
        library.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Merge</h2>
      <p>
        Select related clips and choose <strong>Merge</strong> to group them.
        The original clips stay separate, with each member's content, source and
        date accessible. Use <strong>Unmerge</strong> for an individual member
        or the whole group to return clips to the library.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <h3>Browser capture is not appearing</h3>
      <p>
        Open <strong>All Clips</strong>, clear search or filters and use{' '}
        <strong>Refresh</strong>, or return focus to the library. Check capture
        feedback before retrying: a saved clip may not yet be visible in the
        current view. Quick Search requires Slate to be running.
      </p>
      <h3>Quick Search does not open</h3>
      <p>
        Confirm Slate is running and retry Ctrl + Shift + Space. Restart Slate
        if it still does not open.
      </p>
      <h3>The extension cannot connect</h3>
      <p>
        Confirm Slate Desktop is installed for your Windows account and the
        official extension is installed and enabled. Restart Chrome after
        installation if needed, then try one small synthetic example on a normal
        HTTP/HTTPS page. A missing or blocked native host can be an
        installation, registration or permission problem; it does not prove the
        desktop app was uninstalled. The native host can save while the desktop
        window is closed.
      </p>
      <h3>A save fails</h3>
      <p>
        A storage error is different from a connection error. Check the library
        first, then record the safe error message and contact support if the
        failure continues. Protected browser pages, large selections or
        noncopyable content may not save. Do not repeatedly submit private
        content to diagnose a problem.
      </p>
      <h3>Slate is still running during setup</h3>
      <p>
        Closing the window normally hides Slate in the Windows tray. Save or
        cancel unfinished edits, then choose <strong>Quit</strong> from Slate's
        tray menu. Stop setup using its normal controls if necessary, then retry
        installation after Slate has quit. Do not force-close browsers or
        terminate processes to bypass a maintenance check.
      </p>
      <h3>An update fails</h3>
      <p>
        Keep your installation and data. Check your network connection and the
        safe error message before retrying through Settings. Do not disable
        signature verification or change update endpoints. Do not delete your
        library or choose Delete app data for connection or update errors. An
        older installer does not undo a database migration; recovery may require
        a compatible cold backup.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Platform support</h2>
      <p>
        Slate is available for Windows 11 on Windows x64 (Intel and AMD) and
        Windows ARM64 PCs. Choose the installer for your device.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
      <p>
        Email{' '}
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:support@tryslate.tech">
          support@tryslate.tech
        </a>{' '}
        or use{' '}
        <a
          href={`${site.repositoryUrl}/issues`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          title="Open Slate issues on GitHub in a new tab"
        >
          GitHub issues
        </a>{' '}
        for a public report using a synthetic example. Include what you tried,
        your Windows version and architecture, Slate version, browser and
        extension versions, and the safe error text. Do not send private clip
        content, sensitive URLs, database files, credentials or logs containing
        personal information. For security issues, ask for a private reporting
        route without posting vulnerability details publicly. No response time
        is promised.
      </p>
    </section>
    <a class="text-link" href="/">
      Back to Slate <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
